<title>FINLAND: MERITA SAYS PLANS FRESH 2001 BOND AUCTION.</title>
<headline>MERITA SAYS PLANS FRESH 2001 BOND AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Merita Oy said in a statement on Monday its banking arm Merita Pankki Oy would issue another tranche of 5.5 percent coupon bonds maturing on September 15, 2001 based on bids in an auction on April 17.</p>
<p>&quot;In three earlier auctions, a total of 582 million markka of bonds have been issued,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Bids must be submitted by 1300/1000 GMT on April 17, it said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
